<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>About on</title><link>https://ddbj.github.io/pathogens/en/about/</link><description>Recent content in About on</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://ddbj.github.io/pathogens/en/about/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>About</title><link>https://ddbj.github.io/pathogens/en/about/overview/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ddbj.github.io/pathogens/en/about/overview/</guid><description>&lt;main>
 &lt;div class="container">
 &lt;div class="third-contents">
 &lt;h2>About the portal&lt;/h2>
 &lt;div class="third-contents-inner">
 &lt;p>
This portal is a part of &lt;a href="pathogendatanetwork.org">Pathogen Data Network&lt;/a>, a global consortium coordinated by the
&lt;a href="https://www.sib.swiss/">SIB (Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics&lt;/a>, and is operated by DNA Data Bank of Japan (DDBJ).

The website is built using Hugo on GitHub based on the code of &lt;a href="https://scilifelab.se/data/">SciLifeLab Data Centre&lt;/a>,
and like the original, we make all our codes open source under the MIT licence. 
 &lt;/p>

 &lt;h2>History&lt;/h2>
 &lt;div class="third-contents-inner">
 &lt;p>
An original portal was launched by &lt;a href="https://rcos.nii.ac.jp/">RCOS&lt;/a>
(Research Center for Open Science and Data Platform, National Institute of Informatics)
as "COVID-19 Data Portal Japan" in 2020 in collaboration with other COVID-19 data portals.
The current version started in 2025 as a DDBJ service.
 &lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Feedback</title><link>https://ddbj.github.io/pathogens/en/about/supportfeedback/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ddbj.github.io/pathogens/en/about/supportfeedback/</guid><description>&lt;main>
